{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "root",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -160,
      "y": -620,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# app.py\nComposition root. Every feature module exposes `routes` and an optional `setup(app)`; app.py wires them into one aiohttp app.\n\n`FEATURES = [apps, youtube, opencode, missions, graph, graph_ui, agents_ui, missions_ui, locations_api, mcp, pc_control, schedule, skills_api, setup_ui, voice, power, setup_check, onboarding, integrations, ui]`\n\n`request_security.install(app)` runs last, so it is the first thing a state-changing request meets."
    },
    {
      "id": "g-features",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": -400,
      "width": 1580,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "**hub/features/** — one module per capability, each its own `web.RouteTableDef()`"
    },
    {
      "id": "f-apps",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "### apps.py\nSpawn/stop/proxy the fronted apps (`APPS` registry). Idle reaper. Restart/shutdown endpoints (exit code 42 = relaunch, 0 = stay down)."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-youtube",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -500,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "### youtube.py\nUpload (`yt_upload.py`, YouTube Data API) + download (`ytdl.py`, yt-dlp+ffmpeg). Download pipeline shares lineage with the standalone **yt-fetch** project (same output dirs)."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-opencode",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -220,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "### opencode.py\nPer-folder AI coding sessions. `Manager.create()` copies a source into `Agent Code/<name>[-N]`, writes a source marker, launches `opencode serve` on its own port."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-graph",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "### graph.py\n`/api/graph` — one node per project, auto-discovered (never hand-maintained). Backs the `/graph` D3 UI. Diff/push endpoints for reviewed write-back."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-power",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 340,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 220,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### power.py\nPC power menu (shutdown/restart/sleep/lock).\n\nCommands come from `platforms.power_commands()` — empty off Windows, so every action 404s instead of shelling out to something that is not there.\n\nThe PIN is checked at action time by `power_settings.py` (PBKDF2, changeable without a restart). An empty PIN is a supported, explicit choice."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-ui",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 580,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 220,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "### ui.py\nMenu page, offline/dormant page, service worker, favicons. The only thing that renders the shell UI."
    },
    {
      "id": "g-support",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 70,
      "width": 1270,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "**hub/** — supporting modules every feature can rely on"
    },
    {
      "id": "s-config",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 230,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### config.py\nConstants, `APPS` registry, all paths. `hub/local_settings.py` (gitignored) overrides secrets/PIN/machine paths."
    },
    {
      "id": "s-platform",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -520,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 230,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### platform_win.py\nWindows Job Object — every spawned child process dies with the Hub. Single seam, `_assign_to_job`."
    },
    {
      "id": "s-proxy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -260,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 230,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### proxy.py\nWebSocket-aware streaming reverse proxy. Every fronted app is reached only through this, never directly."
    },
    {
      "id": "s-supervisor",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 230,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### supervisor.py\nStart/stop + idle reaper for proxied apps — spins one up on first request, stops it after inactivity."
    },
    {
      "id": "s-lifecycle",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 260,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 230,
      "height": 120,
      "text": "### lifecycle.py\nStartup hooks, graceful cleanup, force-exit watchdog (bounded shutdown even if something hangs)."
    },
    {
      "id": "g-knowledge",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 500,
      "width": 1090,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "**hub/agent_knowledge/** — the knowledge + status layer OpenCode sessions and the graph both read from"
    },
    {
      "id": "k-init",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 580,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 150,
      "text": "### __init__.py\n`render_agents_md()` — safety rules + wiki-entity summary + skill index, injected into every session's AGENTS.md. Wiki matching: `project_slug` frontmatter first, fuzzy fallback second."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-projects",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -500,
      "y": 580,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 150,
      "text": "### projects.py\n`discover_projects()` — auto-scans `git repositories\\` folder layout, never a static list. `discover_orphan_chats()` — Agent Code folders with no resolvable source."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-status",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -220,
      "y": 580,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 150,
      "text": "### status.py\n`git diff --no-index` per project vs. its copy (Windows-safe). Reviewed push-back: A/M only, never auto-delete. `compute_project_links()` from real `[[wikilinks]]`."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-skills",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 580,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 150,
      "text": "### skills/\nDomain skill files (frontmatter: name/description/keywords), matched against project name + file extensions. Bodies load on demand, not inlined."
    },
    {
      "id": "g-external",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 1060,
      "width": 1480,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "External — not part of this repo, only ever talked to over 127.0.0.1 (or by path)"
    },
    {
      "id": "e-opencode-bin",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "**opencode** binary + `Agent Code\\` copies\nLives OUTSIDE `git repositories\\` on purpose — a session's own working copy can never be mistaken for a source."
    },
    {
      "id": "e-wiki",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -500,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "**LLM Wiki** (this vault)\nRead for AGENTS.md summaries + wiki-link edges. The graph's dashed edges show which projects are/aren't documented here."
    },
    {
      "id": "e-apps",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -220,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "**Fronted apps**\nAny app that binds `127.0.0.1` + honours a base-path env var — e.g. Movie Clipper, File Browser."
    },
    {
      "id": "e-tailscale",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "**Tailscale**\nThe only network path in. The Hub is the sole thing meant to face the tailnet; everything else is proxied."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-missions",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### missions.py\nAutonomous `opencode run` per mission, each in its own git worktree. You review a diff and APPLY (merge) or DISCARD (delete the copy). Your repo is never written to unreviewed.",
      "x": -780,
      "y": -130,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "f-voice",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### voice.py\nTALK: speech in, speech out. From source it imports faster-whisper directly; installed, it shells out to a managed speech runtime so the Hub never carries an ML stack.",
      "x": -500,
      "y": -130,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "f-pc-control",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### pc_control.py + mcp.py\nRoutines the Hub has learned, in a local SQLite under `runtime.STATE`. Control is off until switched on, and every action is approved. Windows-only.",
      "x": -220,
      "y": -130,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "f-onboarding",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### onboarding.py\nFirst-run setup: everything now, or each tool the first time you open it.\n\nIts gating middleware registers **only when PACKAGED** — a git clone must never be redirected into a setup wizard.",
      "x": 60,
      "y": -130,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "f-integrations",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### integrations.py\nNamed, scoped, revocable tokens so scripts and phone shortcuts can call the Hub. Minting is browser-only, so a token can never widen itself.",
      "x": 340,
      "y": -130,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "s-runtime",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### runtime.py\nThe only place that knows source-vs-installed.\n\n`STATE` — repo `hub/` from source, `%LOCALAPPDATA%` installed.\n`python_for(cap)` — managed env, else the running interpreter.\n`PACKAGED` — guards the few genuinely install-only behaviours.\n\nExists so the build never has to patch source.",
      "x": 340,
      "y": 300,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 160
    },
    {
      "id": "s-security",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### request_security.py\nTailscale decides which *devices* can reach the Hub. It cannot decide whether you *meant* a request — any page in your browser can POST.\n\nSo: same-origin for browsers, an integration token for everything else, and reads are never blocked.",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 300,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 160
    },
    {
      "id": "s-platforms",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### platforms.py\nWhat this OS can actually do. macOS and Linux run the same code with a smaller `CAPABILITIES` set, and the UI hides what is missing rather than offering a button that fails.",
      "x": -220,
      "y": 300,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 160
    },
    {
      "id": "g-packaging",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**packaging/** — turning this folder into installers",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 770,
      "width": 1260,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "p-build",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Build-Release.cmd\nDouble-click. Fetches payloads, stages, tests, freezes, compiles the installer. `/all` also tags and pushes so CI builds macOS and Linux.\n\nSee `packaging/BUILDING.md`.",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170
    },
    {
      "id": "p-stage",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### stage_release.py\nAllowlisted copy into a scratch tree — never touches the working Hub — then a privacy audit that refuses any machine path, database or log.\n\nNo source patching, so editing the Hub cannot stale the build.",
      "x": -460,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170
    },
    {
      "id": "p-payloads",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### payloads.json + fetch_payloads.py\nWhat ships inside (Python, yt-dlp, ffmpeg) versus what is fetched when a user asks (MCP, speech, Tailscale, Node, Git).\n\nSizes and hashes are measured, not claimed.",
      "x": -140,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170
    },
    {
      "id": "p-release",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### GitHub Release\nThe only place binaries live. Never the repo.\n\nA public build needs a release-evidence file recording a clean-machine install; Inno also refuses to promote a TEST-ONLY package.",
      "x": 180,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170
    }
  ],
